Imago is the successor to the long-running OLCAO codebase. The
OLCAO (Orthogonalized Linear Combination of Atomic Orbitals)
method was developed at the University of Missouri-Kansas City
and retains its established name; Imago is the rebranded and
re-engineered implementation of it.

If you use Imago in published work, please cite it. Machine-
readable citation metadata is in CITATION.cff at the repository
root.


